# Line-ending normalization (R16 AC8).
#
# The transform engine writes LF unconditionally and records a SHA-256 of every
# output file *as written* in the Build_Manifest. Without this declaration, git's
# core.autocrlf would rewrite text files to CRLF on a Windows checkout, changing
# their bytes and making every checked-out file fail the Build_Manifest hash
# comparison (E_HASH_MISMATCH, R16 AC9). Declaring eol=lf keeps LF on checkout on
# every Supported_Platform, so the manifest hash stays valid everywhere.
#
# This file is a committed repository artifact, not generated output: the
# Transformation_Contract references it via output.gitattributes rather than
# emitting it per build.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Excluded from normalization: the transform must keep these byte-for-byte
# identical to the template source (R10 AC3), so no line-ending transform may
# touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.min.js -text
